<%!-- The settings hub: the one grouped map of everything a member can change
about themselves. The groups come from VutuvWeb.UI.settings_menu/1, the same
source the desktop sidebar renders, so hub and sidebar can never drift apart.
No forms and no destructive control live here; every row is a door to the
focused page.

One list at every width. It used to be two: a grouped list for phones and, on
desktop, a "pick a section from the menu on the left" line that left about
three quarters of the screen empty. The same cards now simply flow into two
columns from md up, which fills the pane and lets someone who does not know our
vocabulary read the whole map at a glance.

Above them sits the filter box (app.js, [data-settings-filter]): it matches each
row's label, its hint line and a list of synonyms (Vutuv's "Sign-in & security"
holds what most people call their password), hides the groups that empty out,
and with JS off simply is not there — the map below works either way. --%>
<.hub_frame user={@user}>
  <div data-settings-map class="space-y-6">
    <div>
      <label for="settings-filter" class="sr-only">{gettext("Search settings")}</label>
      <input
        id="settings-filter"
        type="search"
        data-settings-filter
        autocomplete="off"
        placeholder={gettext("Search settings")}
        class={input_class()}
      />
      <p
        data-settings-empty
        hidden
        class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400"
      >
        {gettext("Nothing here matches. Try another word, or clear the search.")}
      </p>
    </div>

    <%!-- columns, not a grid: the groups are wildly different heights, and a
    grid would leave a ragged gap under every short one. --%>
    <div class="gap-6 md:columns-2 [&>*]:mb-6 [&>*]:break-inside-avoid">
      <section :for={{group, entries} <- settings_menu(@user)} data-settings-group>
        <h2 class="mb-2 px-1 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
          {group}
        </h2>
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-white shadow-sm ring-1 ring-slate-200 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:ring-slate-800">
          <ul class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800">
            <.hub_row :for={entry <- entries} entry={entry} count={@section_counts[entry.key]} />
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</.hub_frame>
